asset.differentiation_notes:
1. Dosing burden: ~2 injections/year vs. 6-8 for Eylea q8w; ~4 for Vabysmo q4m. 2. Real-world: wet AMD patients average only 4-5 injections/year vs. 6-8 recommended;
   EYP-1901 semi-annual dosing could structurally improve adherence and outcomes.
3. Mechanism: small molecule vs. biologic — simpler formulation, no cold chain for the TKI. 4. Phase 2 (DAVIO 2): 67% of patients maintained 6-month dosing with non-inferior BCVA. 5. ACUITY design: non-inferiority vs. q8w aflibercept is a achievable bar given Phase 2 data.
